# Four expressions name a record type plainly enough to read a field against,
# and the table that holds them read three. An annotation says it, a
# constructor pattern's as-binding says it, a local construction says it — and
# `(v):point` says it just as plainly and was not read, so this field read
# compiled clean while the other three were refused where they stand. Both
# engines then refuse it at run time, identically, so what was missing was the
# diagnostic rather than the disagreement.
type point
  x
  y

type other
  z

fn widened v
  p = (v):point
  p.z

pub play = print "{widened (point 1 2)}"
